Kaskad 3: the set of fixes for line 3.1 in amneziawg-linux-kernel-module v3.1.20260906
(archive sha256 e32fa46f1b6f9e319c5261f0b0765c3a9261e40cb7c4616fd73500da961a2932,
commit 4569c4c67f3a57414969260cafbbd04694fbaae0). Set id: kaskad-k31.1.

Why: with HeaderProtectionKey (line 3.1) the tag guards the key with an rw_semaphore that the
receive path takes in softirq; "awg syncconf" under traffic hung a 1 vCPU node within seconds
and panicked a 2 vCPU one (upstream issue #253, no fix upstream on 2026-10-07; Kaskad
laboratory k3/stand/logs/research-awg31-kmod.md, section 3.2). Kaskad's own fix #253 plus
open community pull requests on top of the tag (none merged on 2026-10-07):
  #253 (Kaskad)  rwlock_t + read_lock_bh/write_lock_bh instead of the semaphore; no nested
                 read lock in wg_get_device_dump
  #234           I1-I5 freed after the queues stop (oops on "awg-quick down", #139)
  #235, #236     Jmin > Jmax no longer panics (#254), junk buffer allocation checked
  #237           negative <r/rc/rd -N> refused, total size of I limited
  #238-#240      RejectAfterTime on the data path and after a failed handshake (#227)
  #241           "awg show" of a device with huge I no longer loops (#228)
  #242           classifier: data packets with RandomTrailers are not taken for handshakes (#226)
  #243, #247     netlink dump and key timers hardened
Tested on Ubuntu 24.04 arm64, kernel 6.8: 35 min transit, about 78 000 syncconf with the key
under iperf3, 0 faults (research-awg31-kmod.md, sections 3.2-3.3).

The last hunk is Kaskad's mark: WIREGUARD_VERSION gets "+kaskad-k31.1". DKMS builds with
Kbuild directly, so the mark reaches MODULE_VERSION: /sys/module/amneziawg/version, modinfo
and dmesg ("AmneziaWG 3.1.20260906+kaskad-k31.1 loaded"). Kaskad puts line 3.1 on the module
only when the module in memory carries this mark (lib/kaskad/gw/awgkmod.py, set_loaded).

How Kaskad uses it: awgkmod.py applies it with "patch -p2" inside /usr/src/amneziawg-3.1.20260906
(src/ of the archive), after a "--dry-run", on top of patch #218 when that one is there (both
orders apply cleanly). License: GPL-2.0, the license of the module.

